--TEST--
An `@example` naming a file that is not on disk is `E0324`, because an example nothing compiles rots while the member it documents moves on — `rule:tooling/doc-comment-tags-are-see-and-example`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:tooling/doc-comment-tags-are-see-and-example`: an `@example` names a
// file that exists, and the path is relative to the file that wrote it, as a
// `require` path is.
/// A receipt, and the one file that would show it in use.
///
/// @example examples/nothing-is-here.nvs
final class Receipt {
    public static function total(): int {
        return 0;
    }
}
echo Receipt::total(), "\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0324]: `examples/nothing-is-here.nvs` names no file
  --> %s:7:14
  |
7 | /// @example examples/nothing-is-here.nvs
  |              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ no such file
  = help: the path is relative to the file that wrote it, as a `require` path is

error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
